box('<b>Android update conflict:</b> the same app ID does not guarantee an update. Android also requires an accepted signing certificate. A safe replacement-key migration may require a fresh install and may erase app data. Back up any information you can safely export before removing an app.')
p('<b>Windows installation:</b> Download the standalone EXE, open the file from Downloads, review the Windows security prompt and publisher information, then follow the installer. Choose the install folder if prompted and launch Browz. Do not bypass security warnings unless you have verified the file and understand the risk.')
p('<b>Android installation:</b> Tap the 1.0.3 preview download link, open the downloaded file and allow installs from your browser when Android asks. Because the preview uses the same app ID and signing key as the public build, it installs over an existing Browz installation without uninstalling. If Android reports a signature mismatch, uninstall the old copy first (its data is erased). Android may ask you to allow installs from the download source; remove that permission afterwards. Verify the start page title includes “1.0.3” before relying on the new features (the screenshots in this guide were taken just before that version label was added). Treat it as a test build, not a trusted release.')
sub('Check the file before you install it')
steps('Download the APK and SHA256SUMS.txt from the release page.','On a computer with the repository, run tools/verify-download.sh Browz-Mobile-1.0.3-preview.apk SHA256SUMS.txt. It prints the checksum, verifies the signature and shows the certificate fingerprint.','If the checksum does not match, delete the file. If the fingerprint is the historical one, the script warns you that this build is a preview, not a trusted update.')
p('Windows users can do the same with Get-FileHash and keytool -printcert -jarfile <file>. A valid signature only proves who signed the file; it cannot fix a leaked signing key.','Smallg')
new();h('2  What Browz is for')
p('Browz is an experimental browser: you can open websites, use several tabs, adjust certain privacy settings and inspect some network activity. The desktop and Android apps do not offer the same capabilities.')
