p('Tap the <b>menu</b> (three horizontal lines) to open: New tab, Bookmarks, Find, zoom and video, Privacy controls, Network rules, Containers (separate logins), Hardware &amp; permissions, Request log, Share page, Clear browsing data, and Privacy and limitations. The menu title also shows which container you are in.')
p('Figure 3 was captured before the Network rules, Containers and Hardware entries were added, so it lists fewer items than your build shows.','Smallg')
sub('Do you need an account? No')
p('Browz has no Browz account, no sign-up, no sync and no telemetry. You open the app and browse; there is nothing to sign in to. The “sign in” that matters is the sign-in on the websites you visit, and that is what containers keep apart. Bookmarks, container names, your network rules and a “session open” marker are the only things saved, all in the app’s private storage on this device.')
p('Two honest exceptions: Android WebView Safe Browsing may ask Google whether an address is dangerous (no account involved), and websites obviously see you when you visit them. Browz sends nothing about you to the Browz project because there is no Browz server.')
p('If you never sign in anywhere, you can still use every feature: tabs, containers, network rules, request log, find and zoom.')

sub('Containers: keep two accounts apart')
steps('Tap the menu, then <b>Containers (accounts)</b>. The list shows your containers; the filled circle is the active one.','Tap <b>Switch</b> next to another container. Browz closes every open page, wipes cookies and site storage, and opens a fresh start page in that container.','Sign in to the account you want inside that container. Repeat with the other container for a second account.','Use <b>+ New container</b> to add more spaces (up to 12) and <b>Clear</b> to erase the active one.')
p('Isolation is per container, not per tab: tabs inside one container share cookies. Sessions end when you close Browz, and container data is never written to disk. Switching containers signs you out of the previous one.','Smallg')
sub('Open, switch and close tabs')
steps('Tap the number at the top or <b>Tabs</b> at the bottom.','Choose <b>+ New Tab</b>, or tap a listed tab to switch to it.','Choose <b>Close Active Tab</b> to close the current one. If it is the last tab, the app rotates identity and returns home rather than closing the window.')
p('A <b>Low-cache tab</b> requests less caching, but shares cookies and site storage with other tabs. In the historical APK it is misleadingly called Ghost Tab (RAM); it is not an isolated private session.','Smallg')
